## PART G - SESSION END CHECKLIST

- [ ] Review conversation for lessons/errors
- [ ] Update playbook.md if lessons learned
- [ ] Update state.md if status changed
- [ ] Update data_schema.md if new indicators/terms captured
- [ ] Update setup files if new rules from transcripts
- [ ] Update chart-reader/extraction-protocol.md if refinements made
- [ ] Provide PowerShell commands to write ALL updated files
- [ ] Provide a PowerShell save command and verification for every file
- [ ] Provide session summary + quick start block

### RULE - Circuit Breakers (Non-negotiable)
- Daily loss limit: -3% of capital   ' STOP trading for the day
- Max drawdown: -10% of capital   ' SYSTEM HALT, full re-evaluation required
- Re-validation cadence: Quarterly review of all setup conditions against paper trade data
- Setup kill switch: Any setup whose live performance diverges >20% from backtest   ' immediate suspension

### RULE - PowerShell save commands (Non-negotiable)
Every session that produces or modifies files MUST provide:
  1. PowerShell save command for each modified file
No exceptions. Even for single-file sessions - still provide verification.

